1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,680
在我的生活中，我對這場比賽是最好的。

2
00:00:03,680 --> 00:00:05,000
這場比賽是非常棒的。

3
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:10,000
我可能以為我可以做到35個比賽。

4
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:12,000
但我認為是更好做到55個比賽。

5
00:00:14,760 --> 00:00:18,520
35是場地你試著贏的。

6
00:00:18,520 --> 00:00:22,040
55是場地你開始贏。

7
00:00:22,040 --> 00:00:23,040
來回家

8
00:00:27,400 --> 00:00:28,520
哈囉，朋友們

9
00:00:28,520 --> 00:00:29,760
我是瑞雪

10
00:00:29,760 --> 00:00:31,880
我是一個喜歡全球旅行。

11
00:00:31,880 --> 00:00:34,560
體驗文化和生活的多餘演者。

12
00:00:34,560 --> 00:00:37,800
那剛剛你們聽到的是我和最近新出的電影。

13
00:00:37,800 --> 00:00:39,160
奧德賽的主演

14
00:00:39,160 --> 00:00:41,280
馬特達蒙的對話

15
00:00:41,280 --> 00:00:43,680
我這兩天剛剛從北京回到上海。

16
00:00:43,680 --> 00:00:46,160
是因為我去那邊參加了奧德賽。

17
00:00:46,160 --> 00:00:48,440
在北京舉辦的首映裡。

18
00:00:48,440 --> 00:00:51,440
那天我們在全國最好的IMACS。

19
00:00:51,440 --> 00:00:53,600
畫幅上面看了這部電影。

20
00:00:53,600 --> 00:00:56,640
並且當天導演Christopher Nolan。

21
00:00:56,640 --> 00:00:58,720
他們的製片人Emma Thomas。

22
00:00:58,720 --> 00:01:00,520
以及兩位主演 Matt Damon。

23
00:01:00,520 --> 00:01:03,040
和Charliss Theron都有到達現場。

24
00:01:03,040 --> 00:01:06,280
還舉辦了一場非常精彩的講座。

25
00:01:06,280 --> 00:01:08,760
並且第二天還受到環球的邀請。

26
00:01:08,760 --> 00:01:10,400
和馬特達蒙坐下來。

27
00:01:10,400 --> 00:01:12,120
面對面的聊了聊

28
00:01:12,120 --> 00:01:14,360
我看完電影的感受。

29
00:01:14,360 --> 00:01:17,040
那如果有在小紅書上關注我的朋友。

30
00:01:17,040 --> 00:01:18,640
應該有看到

31
00:01:18,640 --> 00:01:20,920
我從去年開始

32
00:01:20,920 --> 00:01:24,160
有開始經常採訪不同的電影主演。

33
00:01:24,160 --> 00:01:25,560
那這一次

34
00:01:25,560 --> 00:01:27,640
我的感覺非常的不一樣。

35
00:01:27,680 --> 00:01:30,240
因為與其說是一個採訪。

36
00:01:30,240 --> 00:01:34,360
我更覺得他是一個成長福的。

37
00:01:34,360 --> 00:01:36,280
因為馬特達蒙真的是一個。

38
00:01:36,280 --> 00:01:38,360
非常溫柔的人

39
00:01:38,360 --> 00:01:40,560
他看人的眼神非常的真誠。

40
00:01:40,560 --> 00:01:43,040
回答也總是能夠用幾句話。

41
00:01:43,040 --> 00:01:46,240
非常精準的說到重點上。

42
00:01:46,240 --> 00:01:49,600
並且這是我第一次被我的採訪者反問。

43
00:01:49,600 --> 00:01:51,520
問我對我自己提出的問題。

44
00:01:51,520 --> 00:01:53,240
是什麼樣的看法

45
00:01:53,240 --> 00:01:54,640
所以採訪出來之後。

46
00:01:54,640 --> 00:01:58,080
我整個人都覺得非常的輕鬆和充盈。

47
00:01:58,720 --> 00:02:02,080
那麼在跟大家分享採訪片段之前。

48
00:02:02,080 --> 00:02:03,640
我想先簡單介紹一下。

49
00:02:03,640 --> 00:02:05,440
奧德塞的故事背景。

50
00:02:07,080 --> 00:02:09,080
奧德塞奧德塞這個故事。

51
00:02:09,080 --> 00:02:12,640
是西方文學史上最重要的史詩之一。

52
00:02:12,640 --> 00:02:14,920
它是由古希臘式人和馬創作的。

53
00:02:14,920 --> 00:02:16,360
一個神話故事

54
00:02:16,360 --> 00:02:19,040
它的地位大家可以理解為是。

55
00:02:19,040 --> 00:02:20,680
歐洲版的汽油劑

56
00:02:20,680 --> 00:02:22,520
或者是風神堡

57
00:02:22,520 --> 00:02:26,320
這個故事的主角叫做奧德塞奧德塞奧。

58
00:02:26,320 --> 00:02:28,240
他是伊薩卡的國王。

59
00:02:28,240 --> 00:02:31,960
同時也是西臘聯軍中最聰慧的將領之一。

60
00:02:31,960 --> 00:02:35,880
他一直以足之多謀而著名的。

61
00:02:35,880 --> 00:02:38,040
翻譯過來就是我們的朱葛亮。

62
00:02:38,040 --> 00:02:40,640
當他們在打一場非常難的仗的時候。

63
00:02:40,640 --> 00:02:43,000
他想出來了一個非常聰明的技巧。

64
00:02:43,000 --> 00:02:44,920
叫做木馬技

65
00:02:44,920 --> 00:02:46,240
通過他的木馬技

66
00:02:46,240 --> 00:02:48,760
他們成功的攻陷了特洛伊城。

67
00:02:48,760 --> 00:02:51,640
打了一場非常漂亮的勝仗。

68
00:02:51,680 --> 00:02:52,640
打完這個仗

69
00:02:52,640 --> 00:02:55,800
他們就當然說說準備回家了。

70
00:02:55,800 --> 00:02:57,600
卻萬萬沒想到

71
00:02:57,600 --> 00:03:01,360
他在回家的路上遇到了各種各樣的困難。

72
00:03:01,360 --> 00:03:02,600
有被詛咒

73
00:03:02,600 --> 00:03:03,920
有遇到了怪獸

74
00:03:03,920 --> 00:03:05,400
有遇到海妖

75
00:03:05,400 --> 00:03:08,720
還有各種各樣的天災人禍。

76
00:03:08,720 --> 00:03:10,040
所以回家的這一路。

77
00:03:10,040 --> 00:03:12,560
他走了整整20年。

78
00:03:12,560 --> 00:03:14,840
奧德塞這個故事以及這部電影。

79
00:03:14,840 --> 00:03:17,960
講的就是他打完聖上之後。

80
00:03:17,960 --> 00:03:20,160
回家路上的種種經歷。

81
00:03:20,160 --> 00:03:23,720
多的我當然就不跟大家繼續劇透了。

82
00:03:23,720 --> 00:03:26,880
大家如果沒有看過這個故事的話。

83
00:03:26,880 --> 00:03:31,520
我想想一定會被這部電影非常精彩的視覺。

84
00:03:31,520 --> 00:03:35,000
以及這種接二連三的讓人意想不到的。

85
00:03:35,000 --> 00:03:37,320
困難賢族所驚喜到。

86
00:03:37,320 --> 00:03:39,880
那麼接下來我就想跟大家分享。

87
00:03:39,880 --> 00:03:42,240
我和馬特達蒙的對話。

88
00:03:42,240 --> 00:03:45,520
我們幾乎是完全沒有刪減的。

89
00:03:45,520 --> 00:03:49,720
跟大家分享了我們的所聊的所有的話題。

90
00:03:49,720 --> 00:03:51,960
那麼接下來就享受。

91
00:05:49,760 --> 00:05:52,440
因為我們全都在做這部電影。

92
00:05:52,440 --> 00:05:55,280
而且我們覺得這個機會。

93
00:05:55,280 --> 00:05:57,160
我們是第一次 ever try to do。

94
00:05:57,160 --> 00:05:59,040
一部電影就像這部電影。

95
00:05:59,040 --> 00:05:59,560
你知道嗎

96
00:05:59,560 --> 00:06:02,920
然後我們感覺到我們是搜尋者。

97
00:06:02,920 --> 00:06:04,200
我們是第一次去

98
00:06:04,200 --> 00:06:07,640
所以我們有很多的心情。

99
00:06:07,640 --> 00:06:10,480
還有很多的尊敬

100
00:06:10,480 --> 00:06:12,200
為了大家的努力

101
00:06:12,200 --> 00:06:16,040
我認為這部電影是一種。

102
00:06:16,040 --> 00:06:17,680
很 Romantic experience for sure。

103
00:06:17,680 --> 00:06:19,080
還有很多的信心

104
00:06:19,080 --> 00:06:20,080
對

105
00:06:20,080 --> 00:06:23,520
因為我看到的 backstage of the making of the movie。

106
00:06:23,520 --> 00:06:25,960
the huge machines。

107
00:06:25,960 --> 00:06:29,520
all those armors that you brought to Iceland。

108
00:06:29,520 --> 00:06:31,200
to such a place。

109
00:06:31,200 --> 00:06:33,360
Can I ask which month was it?。

110
00:06:33,360 --> 00:06:35,400
That was in June。

111
00:06:35,400 --> 00:06:36,320
June's, okay。

112
00:06:36,320 --> 00:06:37,600
It was there summertime。

113
00:06:37,600 --> 00:06:39,920
but it did not feel like it。

114
00:06:39,920 --> 00:06:40,640
I can imagine。

115
00:06:40,640 --> 00:06:43,520
because Iceland is hard enough just to be there。

116
00:06:43,520 --> 00:06:44,960
Yeah

117
00:06:44,960 --> 00:06:46,640
It's a beautiful country。

118
00:06:47,480 --> 00:06:49,600
I shot there with Chris on Interstellar。

119
00:06:49,600 --> 00:06:51,920
we shot on the glacier。

120
00:06:51,920 --> 00:06:54,480
and it's an incredible place to work。

121
00:06:54,480 --> 00:06:56,320
and really good crews there。

122
00:06:56,320 --> 00:06:58,760
and good people。

123
00:06:58,760 --> 00:07:00,240
but very challenging。

124
00:07:00,240 --> 00:07:02,960
And there was a moment where you were on the boat。

125
00:07:02,960 --> 00:07:06,520
and a dolphin just jumped out from the sea。

126
00:07:06,520 --> 00:07:08,480
and I feel like that's the magic。

127
00:07:08,480 --> 00:07:10,240
Yeah, that's the magic of being out there。

128
00:07:10,240 --> 00:07:12,680
things happen。

129
00:07:12,680 --> 00:07:15,680
and you just are in the real world。

130
00:07:16,680 --> 00:07:19,240
And I feel like you can always see that in a movie。

131
00:07:19,240 --> 00:07:22,800
You can see it in the faces of everybody who's out there。

132
00:07:22,800 --> 00:07:26,400
You know, that it's really the wind and salt water。

133
00:07:26,400 --> 00:07:27,720
and all of that。

134
00:07:27,720 --> 00:07:28,680
You're in the elements。

135
00:07:28,680 --> 00:07:31,520
and that's what this movie needs, right?。

136
00:07:31,520 --> 00:07:33,200
You need to take the audience。

137
00:07:33,200 --> 00:07:35,760
and put them on the journey with the characters。

138
00:07:35,760 --> 00:07:40,120
and that's what that IMAX format does so beautifully。

139
00:07:40,120 --> 00:07:42,000
And you were in there too。

140
00:07:42,000 --> 00:07:45,480
because you were exactly experiencing。

141
00:07:45,640 --> 00:07:47,400
but the characters are experiencing。

142
00:07:47,400 --> 00:07:49,840
Yeah, it makes it a lot easier to do my job。

143
00:07:49,840 --> 00:07:51,640
Yes, I did when I was watching。

144
00:07:51,640 --> 00:07:53,160
I was just thinking。

145
00:07:53,160 --> 00:07:56,400
Man, just let this poor man go home。

146
00:07:56,400 --> 00:07:57,800
All he wants to do is go home。

147
00:07:57,800 --> 00:07:59,560
but there were so many challenges。

148
00:07:59,560 --> 00:08:00,920
one after another。

149
00:08:00,920 --> 00:08:03,320
and usually most stories tell us。

150
00:08:03,320 --> 00:08:05,360
how difficult it is to win。

151
00:08:05,360 --> 00:08:09,600
but Odyssey concentrates on what happens after the victory。

152
00:08:09,600 --> 00:08:14,280
So I wonder why in this story。

153
00:08:14,280 --> 00:08:17,120
Going home is harder than winning。

154
00:08:17,120 --> 00:08:19,400
That's a great question。

155
00:08:19,400 --> 00:08:23,320
And that's been the question since it was written。

156
00:08:23,320 --> 00:08:25,800
What is the aftermath of the victory。

157
00:08:25,800 --> 00:08:27,320
and what does it mean。

158
00:08:27,320 --> 00:08:29,880
and what do you carry。

159
00:08:29,880 --> 00:08:32,320
and to what degree are you accountable。

160
00:08:32,320 --> 00:08:35,080
for the decisions you make。

161
00:08:35,080 --> 00:08:37,920
What does that mean for your life?。

162
00:08:37,920 --> 00:08:39,680
And what it takes to win。

163
00:08:39,680 --> 00:08:41,160
What comes after。

164
00:08:41,240 --> 00:08:43,760
If you don't take accountability。

165
00:08:43,760 --> 00:08:46,440
for what you did just for winning。

166
00:08:46,440 --> 00:08:47,400
That's right。

167
00:08:47,400 --> 00:08:48,760
It's not just about a hero。

168
00:08:48,760 --> 00:08:51,040
It's about everyone。

169
00:08:51,040 --> 00:08:52,200
What are the sacrifices。

170
00:08:52,200 --> 00:08:53,840
that you're willing to take。

171
00:08:53,840 --> 00:08:55,320
That's exactly right。

172
00:08:55,320 --> 00:08:56,960
Yeah, and in fact。

173
00:08:56,960 --> 00:08:57,840
when I first read it。

174
00:08:57,840 --> 00:08:59,120
I said to Chris that。

175
00:08:59,120 --> 00:09:02,400
it reminded me in many ways of Oppenheimer。

176
00:09:02,400 --> 00:09:05,960
and it has some similar themes。

177
00:09:05,960 --> 00:09:07,240
and of course this。

178
00:09:07,240 --> 00:09:10,200
the Odyssey is so rich thematically。

179
00:09:10,280 --> 00:09:12,800
It almost depends on where you are in your life。

180
00:09:12,800 --> 00:09:14,040
when you encounter the story。

181
00:09:14,040 --> 00:09:16,320
because it can be about homecoming。

182
00:09:16,320 --> 00:09:17,480
or family or love。

183
00:09:17,480 --> 00:09:19,880
or war or death or regret。

184
00:09:19,880 --> 00:09:23,560
There's so much in the story。

185
00:09:23,560 --> 00:09:25,000
that depending on。

186
00:09:25,000 --> 00:09:26,480
what you're going through in your life。

187
00:09:26,480 --> 00:09:28,560
or how old you are even。

188
00:09:28,560 --> 00:09:29,960
what your experience has been。

189
00:09:29,960 --> 00:09:32,000
it speaks to you in different ways。

190
00:09:32,000 --> 00:09:34,560
So what is your biggest take away from the story?。

191
00:09:34,560 --> 00:09:36,840
I loved the adaptation that Chris did。

192
00:09:36,840 --> 00:09:40,160
and I was the right。

193
00:09:40,560 --> 00:09:42,280
at the right point in my life。

194
00:09:42,280 --> 00:09:43,720
to take this role on。

195
00:09:43,720 --> 00:09:45,080
it's an amazing role。

196
00:09:45,080 --> 00:09:47,840
and you know。

197
00:09:47,840 --> 00:09:49,800
I probably would have thought。

198
00:09:49,800 --> 00:09:51,120
I could have done it。

199
00:09:51,120 --> 00:09:52,480
when I was 35。

200
00:09:52,480 --> 00:09:55,360
but I think it's better to do it at 55。

201
00:09:55,360 --> 00:09:56,520
when you understand more。

202
00:09:56,520 --> 00:09:57,840
Yeah

203
00:09:57,840 --> 00:09:59,560
and also I kind of feel like。

204
00:09:59,560 --> 00:10:03,320
35 is the stage where you try to win。

205
00:10:03,320 --> 00:10:05,000
and 55 is the stage。

206
00:10:05,000 --> 00:10:07,960
when you are starting to come home。

207
00:10:07,960 --> 00:10:08,760
Yeah, yeah。

208
00:10:09,120 --> 00:10:11,200
I think that's right。

209
00:10:11,200 --> 00:10:12,600
I've definitely felt that shift。

210
00:10:12,600 --> 00:10:13,960
coming into my fifties。

211
00:10:13,960 --> 00:10:16,400
you get a new perspective。

212
00:10:16,400 --> 00:10:18,360
a lot of life is behind you。

213
00:10:18,360 --> 00:10:20,440
and you have a good chance。

214
00:10:20,440 --> 00:10:21,360
to reflect on that。

215
00:10:21,360 --> 00:10:23,120
and really think about。

216
00:10:23,120 --> 00:10:25,400
where you're going。

217
00:10:25,400 --> 00:10:26,840
where do you think you're trying。

218
00:10:26,840 --> 00:10:28,480
to go right now?。

219
00:10:28,480 --> 00:10:30,080
is it easier than odyssey?。

220
00:10:30,080 --> 00:10:32,200
definitely easier than odyssey。

221
00:10:32,200 --> 00:10:33,640
I think

222
00:10:33,640 --> 00:10:35,040
you know I'm very lucky。

223
00:10:35,040 --> 00:10:37,480
with the family that I have。

224
00:10:37,480 --> 00:10:38,720
and the family that we've built。

225
00:10:39,480 --> 00:10:40,840
I have a very clear sense。

226
00:10:40,840 --> 00:10:42,640
of where home is for me。

227
00:10:42,640 --> 00:10:44,560
Oh, that's so beautiful。

228
00:10:44,560 --> 00:10:45,200
Yeah

229
00:10:45,200 --> 00:10:47,720
So I really love。

230
00:10:47,720 --> 00:10:49,520
love the line。

231
00:10:49,520 --> 00:10:50,800
at the end of the movie。

232
00:10:50,800 --> 00:10:52,000
which I actually saw before。

233
00:10:52,000 --> 00:10:53,360
I watch it is。

234
00:10:53,360 --> 00:10:55,360
what you most wanted。

235
00:10:55,360 --> 00:10:57,320
is what you most can have。

236
00:10:57,320 --> 00:10:58,760
and what you most can have。

237
00:10:58,760 --> 00:11:01,880
is what you had but lost。

238
00:11:01,880 --> 00:11:03,160
kind of scares me。

239
00:11:03,160 --> 00:11:04,400
as a 30-year-old。

240
00:11:04,400 --> 00:11:06,640
because I have to be careful。

241
00:11:06,640 --> 00:11:08,120
about what I want。

242
00:11:08,120 --> 00:11:08,560
Yeah

243
00:11:08,560 --> 00:11:10,880
What's your intake about this?。

244
00:11:10,880 --> 00:11:12,680
Well, I'm much more interested。

245
00:11:12,680 --> 00:11:13,320
to hear yours。

246
00:11:13,320 --> 00:11:14,680
That's why I love this。

247
00:11:14,680 --> 00:11:16,000
this part of the process。

248
00:11:16,000 --> 00:11:17,200
where we get to put the movie。

249
00:11:17,200 --> 00:11:18,360
in front of。

250
00:11:18,360 --> 00:11:19,200
in front of people。

251
00:11:19,200 --> 00:11:20,760
and hear how that resonates。

252
00:11:20,760 --> 00:11:21,120
